# The .ko-agent-sandbox/egress/rule of a project that reads one of its own S3 buckets. S3's
# virtual-hosted URL names the bucket in the host, <bucket>.s3.<region>.amazonaws.com, so the
# exact host already admits that bucket and no other; the tree then keeps the reach to one key
# prefix within it, and a key outside — or one spelled with percent-encoding, a dot segment, a
# backslash or an empty segment — is refused and logged. A bucket whose name contains dots does
# not fit S3's wildcard certificate and takes the path-style form instead, where the region's
# host serves every bucket and the bucket is the first segment:
# allow https://s3.<region>.amazonaws.com/<bucket>/ read, the shape gcs-bucket narrows. Reads
# only: a presigned upload URL still fails here, since a PUT is refused where no line grants it.
# What travels in an allowed GET's suffix and query is not bounded; SECURITY.md, "Exfiltration
# through an allowed host".
allow https://my-bucket.s3.us-east-1.amazonaws.com/public/ read
